$ Shallow-water propagation over a submerged bar with DCTA triads that also
$ act between waves from different directions (NONC), on the full circle
$
$ The same bar as triad_dcta.swn, with a wider incident spectrum (a
$ directional spread of 10 degrees) on directions of 10 degrees all round.
$ On a full circle SWDNCTA uses that two directions act on each other in the
$ same way as two that are both turned by a number of bins, and works out
$ the third direction once for every angle between them. That is a choice
$ of this fork for speed: upstream works it out for every pair of
$ directions, and the two differ in rounding only. triad_dcta_nonc_sector.swn
$ has the same directions as a sector, which takes the loop of upstream.
$
PROJECT 'TRIADNON' '001'
SET CARTESIAN
MODE STATIONARY ONEDIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN

CGRID REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 30.0 0.0 300 0 &
      CIRCLE 36 0.10 2.0 31
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0.0 0.0 0.0 30 0 1.0 1.0
READINP BOTTOM 1.0 'bottom.bot' 1 0 FREE

BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDSPEC SIDE WEST CONSTANT PAR 0.06 2.0 0.0 10.0

GEN3 WESTH
OFF WINDGROWTH
OFF WCAPPING
OFF QUADRUPLET
TRIAD DCTA NONC

POINTS 'GAUGES' 2.0 0.0 10.0 0.0 15.0 0.0 18.0 0.0 &
         25.0 0.0 30.0 0.0
TABLE 'GAUGES' HEADER 'triad_dcta_nonc.tbl' XP DEPTH HSIGN TM01 RTP REDTRIAD REDQUAD
SPECOUT 'GAUGES' SPEC1D ABS 'triad_dcta_nonc.spc'
TEST 1 0 POINTS XY 15.0 0.0 S1D 'triad_dcta_nonc_sources.spc'

COMPUTE
STOP
